# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
.pio/
.pioenvs/
.piolibdeps/
*.o
*.elf
*.bin.bak

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# --- runtime data ----------------------------------------------------------
# The database, the cached artwork and the saved recordings. All of it is
# either personal (your collection, your listening history) or rebuildable
# (covers re-download on demand). Neither belongs in a repository.
v2/brain/data/
v2/pi/data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here should ever hold a token, but a stray dotenv is easy to make.
.env
*.token
secrets.json
appletv.json

# --- macOS on exFAT --------------------------------------------------------
# /Volumes/Opslag is exFAT, so macOS writes a "._name" sidecar next to every
# file to hold the metadata the filesystem cannot store. They are invisible in
# Finder, they are not part of the project, and they break C/C++ builds when a
# toolchain globs *.c — see the note in v2/crowpanel/platformio.ini.
._*
.DS_Store
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- editors ---------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- CAD, and version 1 ----------------------------------------------------
# Both live in this directory and neither is published. The enclosure went
# through ten revisions and is still moving; what the shape has to do is in
# v2/BOM.md, which outlives any one of them. Version 1 is the simple knob this
# grew out of and is kept for reference, not as something to build.
#
# They were in this repository once and were taken back out of its history on
# 7 August 2026, together with a few reference models — a Pi Zero mesh alone was
# 24 MB, against 600 kB for the whole of the rest. Ignored rather than deleted
# so that putting them back is a decision, not an accident.
3D Print/
Housing/
*.stl
*.step
*.f3d
*.3mf
/src/
/platformio.ini
/BOM.md
/docs/version-1.md
